From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:54:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/44] minimize: Firefox counts from closed windows, all
 running profiles, ambiguous shared titles

Review fixes for the tab-count matching:
- A blank window takes only the session window it took before, so a new
  blank window does not take a closed window's count.
- A stale session window qualifies only when one of the windows showed
  its selected title lately, so a new window does not take a closed one's.
- A Firefox count is unlisted when no session window is on that page; a
  background tab or tab history no longer keeps it.
- A terminal or Files title shared by windows with different counts drops
  the count; shared titles with the same count keep it.
- The session files of all running profiles are read and merged.
- A window whose selected tab has no page stays in the session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

